# The Recommended rule of the same name holds the idioms. Docs use
# these four often, and each mostly reads one way, so they sit here as
# suggestions. `set up` covers install, configure, and create, and the
# one-word verb says which (`configure the remote`). `clean up`
# becomes delete or remove, `show up` becomes appear, and `turn into`
# becomes become. The nouns `setup` and `cleanup` are one word and
# pass.
expr main [([set, sets, setting] up), ([clean, cleans, cleaned, cleaning] up), ([show, shows, showed, shown, showing] up), ([turn, turns, turned, turning] into)]
let message "Phrasal verb. Use one verb, such as configure, delete, appear, or become."
let description "Flags set up, clean up, show up, and turn into, which one plain verb often replaces."
let becomes ""
let kind "Style"
allows "The setup script installs the hooks."
allows "The cleanup job deletes old builds."
